"private":false,"owner":{"login":"geoalchemy","id":851855,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjg1MTg1NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/851855?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoalchemy","html_url":"https://github.com/geoalchemy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoalchemy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoalchemy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoalchemy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoalchemy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoalchemy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoalchemy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoalchemy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoalchemy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoalchemy/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2","description":"Geospatial extension to SQLAlchemy","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/deployments","created_at":"2012-09-01T10:00:24Z","updated_at":"2025-12-03T03:12:10Z","pushed_at":"2025-11-18T15:01:25Z","git_url":"git://github.com/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:geoalchemy/geoalchemy2.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2","homepage":"http://geoalchemy-2.readthedocs.org","size":1150,"stargazers_count":689,"watchers_count":689,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":120,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":12,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":120,"open_issues":12,"watchers":689,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"I'm seeing some breaking behaviors when using geoalchemy2 in combination with SQLAlchemy 1.4.21+ as it relates to the wrapping of columns with PostGIS conversion functions.\r\n\r\nGiven the code below:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom geoalchemy2.types import Geometry\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Table, Column, MetaData, Text\r\n\r\n\r\nclass RawGeometry(Geometry):\r\n    def column_expression(self, col: Column):\r\n        return col\r\n\r\n\r\nmd = MetaData()\r\nMyTable = Table(\r\n    \"my_table\",\r\n    md,\r\n    Column(\"name\", Text),\r\n    # Just adding a sanity check here that uses a \"raw\" geometry column per the docs\r\n    Column(\"raw_geometry\", RawGeometry(srid=4326)),\r\n    Column(\"geometry\", Geometry(srid=4326)),\r\n)\r\n\r\n\r\nq = (\r\n    MyTable.insert()\r\n    .values(\r\n        {\"name\": \"test\", \"raw_geometry\": \"Doesn't matter\", \"geometry\": \"Doesn't matter\"}\r\n    )\r\n    .returning(MyTable)\r\n)\r\n\r\nprint(q)\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen running using geoalchemy2 @ v0.12.5 and SQLAlchemy @ v1.4.20, I get the following output:\r\n\r\n```\r\nINSERT INTO my_table (name, raw_geometry, geometry) VALUES (:name, ST_GeomFromEWKT(:raw_geometry), ST_GeomFromEWKT(:geometry))\r\nRETURNING my_table.name, my_table.raw_geometry, ST_AsEWKB(my_table.geometry) AS geometry\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote how the `ST_AsEWKB(my_table.geometry)` is correctly labeled with `geometry` in the `RETURNING` clause.\r\n\r\nHowever, when running using geoalchemy2 @ v0.12.5 and SQLAlchemy @ v1.4.21, I get the following output:\r\n\r\n```\r\nINSERT INTO my_table (name, raw_geometry, geometry) VALUES (:name, ST_GeomFromEWKT(:raw_geometry), ST_GeomFromEWKT(:geometry))\r\nRETURNING my_table.name, my_table.raw_geometry, ST_AsEWKB(my_table.geometry) AS geometry_1\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote how instead here the `ST_AsEWKB(my_table.geometry)` is incorrectly labeled with `geometry_1` in the `RETURNING` clause.\r\n\r\nHas anyone else run into this problem? AFAICT this only happens in a `RETURNING` clause, as doing something like `print(MyTable.select())` shows the same correctly-labeled `geometry` column across both versions.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/issues/409/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/geoalchemy/geoalchemy2/issues/409/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1306241259","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/8770#issuecomment-1306241259","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/8770","id":1306241259,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85N26jr","user":{"login":"jerluc","id":745427,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NTQyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/745427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc","html_url":"https://github.com/jerluc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-11-07T21:45:19Z","updated_at":"2022-11-07T21:45:19Z","body":"@zzzeek being new to the internals of this codebase, this was where I was able to fix the above test example while still ensuring no pre-existing unit tests fail:\r\n\r\n```patch\r\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/compiler.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/compiler.py\r\nindex 704c0d19c..72fb14b6d 100644\r\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/compiler.py\r\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/compiler.py\r\n@@ -3789,6 +3789,7 @@ class SQLCompiler(Compiled):\r\n                     column._tq_label,\r\n                 ),\r\n             )\r\n+\r\n         else:\r\n             # determine here whether this column should be rendered in\r\n             # a labelled context or not, as we were given no required label\r\n@@ -3799,6 +3800,8 @@ class SQLCompiler(Compiled):\r\n                 # type-specific expression wrapping the given column,\r\n                 # so we render a label\r\n                 render_with_label = True\r\n+                if isinstance(column.type, sqltypes.TypeDecorator):\r\n+                    fallback_label_name = column.name\r\n             elif isinstance(column, elements.ColumnClause):\r\n                 # table-bound column, we render its name as a label if we are\r\n                 # inside of a subquery only\r\n```\r\n\r\nBeing honest though, I'm a bit uncertain about a few things:\r\n\r\n- `fallback_label_name` was convenient and works, but I'm not sure if this is the right variable to reuse for this purpose\r\n- Is `TypeDecorator` the right type to check for? Or is this making too broad of an assumption that all `TypeDecorator`s intend to wrap columns in column expressions that would need to be relabeled?\r\n- Another attempt I made was to manipulate `col_expr` itself by wrapping it in something like `Label(column.name, col_expr)`; this also worked, but I'm not sure if this breaks other behaviors that might introspect `col_expr`\r\n- You mentioned in geoalchemy/geoalchemy2#409 that there's a possibility this will all change again in SQLAlchemy 2.0; while it'd be great (for me at least) to get a patch in for 1.4, I'd also love to hear more about how you see 2.0 better handling this scenario","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1306241259/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jerluc","id":745427,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NTQyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/745427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc","html_url":"https://github.com/jerluc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jerluc/